y, Mike Minogue prepare to face off in Thursday night debate", "source": "Boston Herald", "published": "2026-10-07T22:30:44+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirgFBVV95cUxNRnBncFlhU0RuM1lFVUM5bTlNbHc5Zm5QLUxsLTVWZmZhMVpKZTQ2dVNjcm1NZmZrRDMzazliQTZkNG42TERiTm5reHdaSy1kRy1SU1NvVVhpb2F0UlFiVE41d0cxYmNIRThENDRhTVpXNURxUWpuY0xfWnVSRzNwQkRSTzgwVlQ0YWY4b0RwbURtcTdPMVI3V0NBcGVjMTlzTVluXzAzeS11WE1pZnc?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 17.08, "prior_sd": 5.34, "poll_margin": 19.62, "poll_sd": 6.39, "poll_weight": 0.41, "fundamentals": {"margin": 18.7, "lean": 10.5, "environment": 4.2, "incumbency": 4.0, "money": 0.0}, "rating_margin": 16.0, "sigma_race": 5.0, "sigma_total": 5.46, "baseline_margin": 18.13, "analyst_adjustment": 0.87, "key_factors": ["Healey's incumbency in a D+14 state", "Consistent 19-21 point polling leads all cycle", "All seven expert ratings call it Solid/Safe D", "Markets price Healey at 95-96%"], "rationale": "Every poll this cycle shows Healey ahead by 17 to 27 points, and the recent MassINC and UNH surveys still put her up 16 to 21 even as Minogue's pitch on the economy struggles to land. With a D+14 baseline, unanimous Solid/Safe D ratings, and markets at 95-96%, the race stays firmly in Safe D territory.", "watch": "A major late scandal or an affordability-driven backlash shifting the polls by double digits would be needed to put this in play.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Maura Healey (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Maura Healey seeks a second term in a state that leans Democratic by about 14 points, facing Republican businessman Mike Minogue and an independent candidate. Polling has been remarkably stable all year, with Healey leading by 17 to 27 points in every survey, including recent September polls from MassINC and UNH showing margins of 16 to 21 points. All seven expert raters classify the race as Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets give Healey a 95 to 96 percent chance of winning.\